e.","anchor":"cldf2-11068"},{"id":"cldf2-11069","tx":"Mari adan toula.","sg":["Mari","adan","tou-la."],"gl":["Mary","in","hole-DEF"],"tl":"Mary is in the hole.","anchor":"cldf2-11069"},{"id":"cldf2-11070","tx":"I halé Mari vini andèwò a toula.","sg":["I","halé","Mari","vini","andèwò","a","tou-la."],"gl":["3SG","pull","Mary","come","outside","PREP","hole-DEF"],"tl":"He pulled Mary out of the hole.","anchor":"cldf2-11070"},{"id":"cldf2-11169","tx":"Timounla té ka pléré, manmany mennéy alé.","sg":["Timoun-la","té","ka","pléré,","manman-y","menné-y","alé."],"gl":["child-DEF","PST","PROG","cry","mother-POSS","take-it","go"],"tl":"The child cried, his mother took him along (away from the speaker).","anchor":"cldf2-11169"},{"id":"cldf2-11253","tx":"I pwan vwati touché Lapwent.","sg":["I","pwan","vwati","touché","Lapwent."],"gl":["3SG","take","car","arrive","La.Pointe"],"tl":"S/he went to La Pointe by car.","anchor":"cldf2-11253"},{"id":"cldf2-11331","tx":"I maké on lèt ba Jòj.","sg":["I","maké","on","lèt","ba","Jòj."],"gl":["3SG","write","INDF","letter","give","George"],"tl":"He/She wrote a letter to George.","anchor":"cldf2-11331"},{"id":"cldf2-11332","tx":"Ijénie ka pòté mango ba Ijenn.","sg":["Ijénie","ka","pòté","mango","ba","Ijenn."],"gl":["Eugénie","PROG","bring","mango","to","Eugène"],"tl":"Eugénie is bringing the mangos to Eugène.","anchor":"cldf2-11332"},{"id":"cldf2-11465","tx":"I ka débouyé'y.","sg":["I","ka","débouyé'y."],"gl":["3SG","PROG","manage.3SG"],"tl":"He does well.","anchor":"cldf2-11465"},{"id":"cldf2-11466","tx":"I ka débouyé kò a'y.","sg":["I","ka","débouyé","kò","a'y."],"gl":["3SG","PROG","manage","body","PREP.3SG"],"tl":"He does well.","anchor":"cldf2-11466"},{"id":"cldf2-11467","tx":"I dépann kò a'y.","sg":["I","dépann","kò","a'y."],"gl":["3SG","kill","body","PREP.3SG"],"tl":"He killed himself.","anchor":"cldf2-11467"},{"id":"cldf2-11468","tx":"I ka gadé limenm adan glasla.","sg":["I","ka","gadé","li-menm","adan","glas-la."],"gl":["3SG","PROG","look","3SG-EMPH","in","mirror-DEF"],"tl":"She is looking at herself in the mirror.","anchor":"cldf2-11468"},{"id":"cldf2-11718","tx":"Yo ka gadé yomenm.","sg":["Yo","ka","gadé","yo-menm."],"gl":["3PL","PROG","look","3PL-EMPH"],"tl":"They are looking at themselves.","anchor":"cldf2-11718"},{"id":"cldf2-11719","tx":"Yonn ka gadé lòt.","sg":["Yonn","ka","gadé","lòt."],"gl":["one","PROG","look","other"],"tl":"They are looking at each other.","anchor":"cldf2-11719"},{"id":"cldf2-11720","tx":"Yo bo.","sg":["Yo","bo."],"gl":["3PL","kiss"],"tl":"They kissed (each other).","anchor":"cldf2-11720"},{"id":"cldf2-11853","tx":"Chanmla ja baléyé.","sg":["Chanm-la","ja","baléyé."],"gl":["room-DEF","already","swept.up"],"tl":"The room has already been swept up.' (The only kind of passive attested in Guadeloupean Creole is a passive with no agent and with no overt marking on the verb. See also Ludwig et al. (2002: 31).)","anchor":"cldf2-11853"},{"id":"cldf2-12026","tx":"Mwen konnèt on ti boutik ki ka vann bèbèl kréyòl.","sg":["Mwen","konnèt","on","ti","boutik","ki","ka","vann","bèbèl","kréyòl."],"gl":["1SG","know","INDF","little","shop","REL","PROG","sell","fancy.jewels","creole"],"tl":"I know a little shop which sells creole fancy jewels.","anchor":"cldf2-12026"},{"id":"cldf2-12027","tx":"Sé madanmla ka maré paké kannla ka chanté.","sg":["Sé","madanm-la","ka","maré","paké","kann-la","ka","chanté."],"gl":["DEF.PL","woman-DEF","PROG","tie","package","sugar.cane-DEF","PROG","sing"],"tl":"The women who are tying the sugar cane packages are singing.","anchor":"cldf2-12027"},{"id":"cldf2-12028","tx":"Sé madanmla i ka maré paké kannla ka chanté.","sg":["Sé","madanm-la","i","ka","maré","paké","kann-la","ka","chanté."],"gl":["DEF.PL","woman-DEF","RES","PROG","tie","package","surgar.cane-DEF","PROG","sing"],"tl":"The women who are tying the sugar cane packages are singing.' (The resumptive pronoun i can be used for all persons. For further discussion, see Ludwig (1996: 305ff).)","anchor":"cldf2-12028"},{"id":"cldf2-12182","tx":"Mi on bouké flè manman mwen ka voyé ba'w.","sg":["Mi","on","bouké","flè","manman","mwen","ka","voyé","ba'w."],"gl":["here","INDF","bunch.of","flowers","mother","1SG.POSS","PROG","send","for.2SG"],"tl":"Here is a bunch of flowers which my mother sent to you.","anchor":"cldf2-12182"},{"id":"cldf2-12183","tx":"Ektò vann flè ki Jènvyèv platné lanné pasé.","sg":["Ektò","vann","flè","ki","Jènvyèv","platné","lanné","pasé."],"gl":["Hector","sell","flower","REL","Geneviève","plant","year","last"],"tl":"Hector sold the flowers that Geneviève planted last year.","anchor":"cldf2-12183"},{"id":"cldf2-12309","tx":"koutola ou ka sèvi épi'y la","sg":["kouto-la","ou","ka","sèvi","épi'y","la"],"gl":["knife-DEF","2SG","use","cut","with.3SG","DET"],"tl":"the knife you use (the knife with which you cut)","anchor":"cldf2-12309"},{"id":"cldf2-12457","tx":"I di i ké vini.","sg":["I","di","i","ké","vini."],"gl":["3SG","say","3SG","FUT","come"],"tl":"He said he will come.","anchor":"cldf2-12457"},{"id":"cldf2-12458","tx":"ou ka di yo pa'a ni tan travay","sg":["ou","ka","di","yo","pa'a","ni","tan","travay"],"gl":["2SG","IPFV","say","3PL","NEG.IPFV","have","time","work"],"tl":"You say that they don't have time to work.","anchor":"cldf2-12458"},{"id":"cldf2-12459","tx":"Yo diy konha nou kay bengné nou.","sg":["Yo","di-y","konha","nou","kay","bengné","nou."],"gl":["3PL","say-3SG","like.that","1PL","go","bath","1PL"],"tl":"They said to him we would take a bath.' (Konha is a variant of konsa.The complementizer konha seems to belong to the register of elder generations.)","anchor":"cldf2-12459"},{"id":"cldf2-12460","tx":"I dimwen konmkwa i pé ké la jòdla.","sg":["I","di-mwen","konmkwa","i","pé","ké","la","jòd-la."],"gl":["3SG","tell-1SG.OBJ","COMP","3SG","NEG.FUT","FUT","there","day-DET"],"tl":"He told me that he would not be there today.' (The complementizer konmkwa seems to belong to elder generation registers. Pé is a special negative particle used in combinat